# onnxruntime-node's postinstall script downloads the optional CUDA execution-provider
# binaries on Linux/x64. The upstream release URL for the pinned version returns 404,
# which makes `npm ci` fail on every Linux x64 environment (GitHub Actions runners and
# Vercel's build containers alike).
#
# The CPU binaries are bundled inside the package, and this project never uses the CUDA
# execution provider - the browser build uses onnxruntime-web/WASM and the Node
# evaluation engine uses the bundled CPU binary. Skipping the CUDA download is therefore
# correct here and keeps `npm ci` reproducible.
#
# Reference: node_modules/onnxruntime-node/script/install.js (ONNXRUNTIME_NODE_INSTALL_CUDA)
onnxruntime-node-install-cuda=skip
